  "info": {
    "title": "Make-to-order line (library assets)",
    "category": "Manufacturing",
    "description": "A small make-to-order line built entirely from Manufacturing 1.0.0 assets, and deliberately still on those v1 definitions (the library has a 2.0.0 since). Jobs are released every 6 minutes into a CONWIP loop of 12 tokens, baked four to a load, machined, then inspected -- 85% pass, 10% go back to the machine, 5% are scrapped, and every job gives its token back whichever way it leaves. All four resources run at 60-85%, so the queues, the rework loop and the oven's batching are all visible in the results."
  },
